# Git's automatic line-ending conversion rewrites bytes on checkout. This
# project hashes files it tracks: the pinned interpreter tarball, every
# capture in runs.yaml, the fixture mission, and model/.manifest. A Windows
# working tree with conversion on would break all of them against a file
# nobody edited.
#
# Turn conversion off for everything. Files stay exactly as committed, on
# both platforms, and a hash means what it says.
* -text

# Shell scripts need LF whatever an editor does to them.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Missions are zip files.
*.miz binary
